    fix: Handle back button in modal image gallery to prevent app closure
    
    Implemented proper back button handling for the modal image gallery displayed
    when viewing location photos, preventing unexpected app closure and providing
    intuitive navigation behavior.
    
    Issue:
    When viewing location images in the modal gallery (opened by tapping the camera
    icon on a location card), pressing the device back button would close the entire
    app instead of just closing the modal overlay. This violated Android navigation
    patterns and created a poor user experience.
    
    Solution:
    Implemented OnBackPressedCallback to intercept back button presses when the
    modal gallery is visible and close only the modal instead of the activity.
    
    Technical Implementation:
    - Added OnBackPressedCallback as a class property in MainActivity
    - Callback initially disabled (isEnabled = false)
    - Handles back press by:
      * Hiding imageGalleryOverlay (setting visibility to GONE)
      * Showing FAB buttons (addLocationFab and quickLocationButton)
      * Callback automatically disables itself after handling
    
    Lifecycle Management:
    - Callback registered in onCreate() via onBackPressedDispatcher.addCallback()
    - Enabled when modal opens (backPressedCallback.isEnabled = true)
    - Disabled when modal closes via:
      * Toolbar navigation click (close button)
      * Overlay click (tap outside)
      * Back button press (in callback handler itself)
    
    User Experience:
    Before Fix:
    - Open location → tap camera icon → view images → press back → app closes ❌
    
    After Fix:
    - Open location → tap camera icon → view images → press back → modal closes ✓
    - Location list remains visible
    - User can continue browsing locations
    - Consistent with Android back navigation patterns
    
    Modal Closing Methods (all now work consistently):
    1. Toolbar back button (X icon)
    2. Tap overlay background
    3. Device back button (NEW)
    
    Modified Files:
    - MainActivity.kt - Added OnBackPressedCallback and enable/disable logic
    
    Dependencies:
    - androidx.activity.OnBackPressedCallback (modern back press handling)
    - Replaces deprecated onBackPressed() method
    - Works with Android's predictive back gesture (Android 13+)

